  "therapist": "Clients who are extremely distressed are one of the most difficult tasks for therapists to handle in a therapy session. What you just saw in the video there was an attempt by myself to assist Danielle through some very distressing events that have been going on for her, specifically a breakup with her boyfriend. One of the things that I hope you did see in that short vignette that you just saw was that although the therapist at some times was engaged with the client and was being somewhat empathic, the therapist was also very, very keen to move off topic, found the distress that the client was showing very difficult to tolerate and was very keen to move away from that subject matter. And even though the client continually pulled the therapy session back to the discussion of her own flaws and the problems with the breakup with her boyfriend, the therapist really wasn't getting the message there and persisted in trying to derail what the client wanted to talk about and move the content of the session away from the breakup with the boyfriend.",
